== Electoral campaigns ==

=== Nationalist Republican Alliance ===


On 27 October 2017, {{ill|Mauricio Interiano|es|Mauricio Interiano}}, the president of the Nationalist Republican Alliance, announced that the party would hold its primary election on 22 April 2018.<ref name="ARENAMI">{{cite web|url=http://elmundo.sv/arena-elegira-aspirante-a-presidencia-22-abril-de-2018/|title=ARENA Elegirá Aspirante a Presidencia 22 Abril de 2018|trans-title=ARENA Will Elect Those Who Aspire the Presidency on 22 April 2018|language=es|date=28 October 2017|access-date=2 April 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|first1=Edgardo|last1=Rivera|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180407120219/http://elmundo.sv/arena-elegira-aspirante-a-presidencia-22-abril-de-2018/|archive-date=7 April 2018|url-status=dead}}</ref> Six members of the party expressed interest in securing the party's presidential nomination:<ref name="ARENAMI" /><ref name="LPGa">{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Gerardo-Awad-y-Rafael-Montalvo-quedan-fuera-de-competencia-por-candidatura-presidencial-en-ARENA-20171219-0028.html|title=Gerardo Awad y Rafael Montalvo Quedan Fuera de Competencia por Candidatura Presidencial en ARENA|trans-title=Gerardo Awad and Rafael Montalvo Remain Outside of Competition for ARENA's Presidential Candidacy|language=es|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|date=19 December 2017|access-date=2 April 2019}}</ref>

* Gerardo Awad, businessman
* [[Carlos Calleja]], businessman
* [[Gustavo López Davidson|Gustavo López]], businessman
* [[Rafael Montalvo (politician)|Rafael Montalvo]], former deputy of the Legislative Assembly
* [[Luis Parada (lawyer)|Luis Parada]], lawyer
* [[Javier Simán]], businessman

In October 2017, Parada withdrew his candidacy, believing that his campaign would be impossible.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/Abogado-Luis-Parada-deja-lucha-por-candidatura-presidencial-de-ARENA--20171002-0068.html|title=Abogado Luis Parada Deja Lucha por Candidatura Presidencial de ARENA|trans-title=Lawyer Luis Parada Quits Fighting for ARENA's Presidential Candidacy|language=es|date=2 October 2017|access-date=30 July 2023|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]}}</ref> In December 2017, Awad and Montalvo were eliminated from competition, while Calleja, Simán, and López advanced to the party's primary election<ref name="LPGa" /> where Calleja won 60.8 percent of the vote, officially becoming the party's presidential nominee.<ref name="CallejaNom">{{cite web|url=https://historico.elsalvador.com/historico/473612/carlos-calleja-candidato-presidencial-de-arena-para-elecciones-2019.html|title=Carlos Calleja, Candidato Presidencial de ARENA para Elecciones 2019|trans-title=Carlos Calleja, Presidential Candidate of ARENA for the 2019 Elections|language=es|date=22 April 2018|access-date=2 April 2023|work=[[El Diario de Hoy|El Salvador.com]]}}</ref>

