=== Farabundo Martí National Liberation Front ===

On 28 February 2018, the Farabundo Martí National Liberation Front announced that it would hold its primary election on 27 May 2018.<ref name="LPGFMLM">{{cite web|url=https://www.laprensagrafica.com/elsalvador/FMLN-convoca-a-eleccion-interna-para-candidato-presidencial-cupula-ya-apoyo-a-Gerson-Martinez-20180228-0065.html|title=FMLN Convoca a Elección Interna para Candidato Presidencial; Cúpula ya Apoyó a Gerson Martínez|trans-title=FMLN Calls for Internal Election for Presidential Candidate; Cúpula Already Supported Gerson Martínez|date=28 February 2018|access-date=2 April 2023|language=es|work=[[La Prensa Gráfica]]|first1=Cristian|last1=Meléndez}}</ref><ref name="ESFMLN">{{cite web|url=https://historico.elsalvador.com/historico/469917/fmln-convoca-a-inscripcion-de-precandidatos-a-la-presidencia.html|title=FMLN Convoca a Inscripción de Precandidatos a la Presidencia|trans-title=FMLN Convokes the Inscription of Pre-Candidates to the Presidency|language=es|date=11 April 2018|access-date=2 April 2023|work=[[El Diario de Hoy|El Salvador.com]]}}</ref> [[Óscar Ortiz (Salvadoran politician)|Óscar Ortiz]], the then vice president of El Salvador, was a potential candidate to secure the party's nomination, but he declined to run after Salvador Cerén appointed him as the technical secretary of the presidency.<ref name="ESFMLN" /> Two party members announced their intention to seek the party's presidential nomination:<ref name="ESFMLN" /><ref name="HMpre">{{cite web|url=http://elmundo.sv/hugo-martinez-se-inscribe-como-precandidato-presidencial-para-internas-del-fmln/|title=Hugo Martínez se Inscribe como Precandidato Presidencial para Internas del FMLN|trans-title=Hugo Martínez Inscribes Himself as a Presidential Pre-Candidate for the FMLN's Internal Elections|language=es|date=23 April 2018|access-date=2 April 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|archive-date=23 April 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180423212908/http://elmundo.sv/hugo-martinez-se-inscribe-como-precandidato-presidencial-para-internas-del-fmln/|url-status=bot: unknown}}</ref>

* {{ill|Gerson Martínez (politician){{!}}Gerson Martínez|es|Gerson Martínez (El Salvador)}}, former deputy of the Legislative Assembly
* [[Hugo Martínez (politician)|Hugo Martínez]], [[Minister of Foreign Affairs (El Salvador)|minister of foreign affairs]] (2014–2018)

On 27 May 2018, Hugo Martínez was selected as the party's presidential nominee, winning 72.09 percent of the vote.<ref name="FMLNres">{{cite web|url=http://elmundo.sv/hugo-martinez-gano-con-20259-votos-en-el-fmln/|title=Hugo Martínez Gano con 20,259 Votos en el FMLN|trans-title=Hugo Martínez Won with 20,559 Votes in the FMLN|language=es|date=27 May 2018|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]|access-date=3 April 2023|archive-date=21 April 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190421021730/https://elmundo.sv/hugo-martinez-gano-con-20259-votos-en-el-fmln/|url-status=dead}}</ref> The party elected [[Karina Sosa]], a former deputy of the Legislative Assembly, as the party's vice presidential nominee.<ref name="FMLN PCN">{{cite web|url=http://elmundo.sv/fmln-y-pcn-ratifican-a-sus-candidatas-a-vicepresidenta/|title=FMLN y PCN Ratifican a Sus Candidatas a Vicepresidenta|trans-title=FMLN and PCN Ratify Their Candidates for Vice President|language=es|date=27 May 2018|access-date=2 April 2023|work=[[El Mundo (El Salvador)|El Mundo]]}}</ref>

