== Debates ==

Two presidential debates were held; the first was hosted by the [[University of El Salvador]] (UES) on 16 December 2018 and the second was hosted by the {{ill|Salvadoran Association of Broadcasters|es|Asociación Salvadoreña de Radiodifusores}} (ASDER). Calleja, Martínez, and Alvarado attended both debates, while Bukele was absent from both.<ref name="debate 1">{{cite web|url=https://historico.elsalvador.com/historico/549666/en-directo-debate-presidencial-en-la-universidad-de-el-salvador.html|title=Candidatos a la Presidencia Debatieron en la Universidad de El Salvador|trans-title=Presidential Candidates Debated in the University of El Salvador|language=es|date=16 December 2018|access-date=2 April 2023|work=[[El Diario de Hoy|El Salvador.com]]|first1=V.|last1=Jurado|first2=Ricardo|last2=Avelar}}</ref><ref name="debate 2">{{cite web|url=https://historico.elsalvador.com/historico/557667/en-vivo-tres-candidatos-presidenciales-plantean-sus-propuestas-en-el-debate-de-asder.html|title=Tres Candidatos Presidenciales Plantearon Sus Propuestas en el Debate de ASDER|trans-title=Three Presidential Candidates Raised Their Proposals in the ASDER Debate|language=es|date=13 January 2019|access-date=2 April 2023|first1=R.|last1=Tejada|first2=Ricardo|last2=Avelar|work=[[El Diario de Hoy|El Salvador.com]]}}</ref>

